---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Terms of Use | Skill Foundry" description="Terms of use for Skill Foundry resources and website content.">
  <section class="page-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">TERMS</p>
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p>These terms describe the general use of the Skill Foundry website and its educational resources.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow article-content">
      <h2>Use of resources</h2>
      <p>Skill Foundry provides prompts, tutorials, workflows and related educational material for practical learning and experimentation. You are responsible for how you use the resources and for reviewing the rules and policies of any third-party tool you use with them.</p>

      <h2>No guarantee of results</h2>
      <p>AI tools can change their models, features and outputs over time. Resources are provided for educational purposes and do not guarantee a particular result, accuracy, availability or suitability for a specific project.</p>

      <h2>Third-party services</h2>
      <p>Links or tutorials may reference third-party websites and tools. Skill Foundry does not control those services and is not responsible for their availability, policies, content or results.</p>

      <h2>Content and availability</h2>
      <p>Website content may be updated, replaced or removed as the library evolves. Skill Foundry aims to keep resources useful and accurate, but the website is provided on an ongoing basis without a promise that every page or feature will always be available.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>For questions about the website or its content, use the contact method provided through Skill Foundry's official social presence.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
